# Migration SQL is embedded verbatim and its SHA-256 is recorded in every
# database's ledger. A checkout that rewrote these files to CRLF would embed
# different bytes, and a database migrated by that build would then be refused
# by an official build as ErrMigrationDrift. The checksum canonicalises line
# endings as well (see Migration.Checksum) — this keeps the working tree itself
# identical everywhere, so the SQL that runs is byte-for-byte the reviewed SQL.
internal/core/storage/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
internal/core/storage/migrations/testdata/*.sql text eol=lf
